From: Stijn Tintel <stijn@linux-ipv6.be>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 18:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: do not assist learning between same-parent ports

DSA considers every bridge port which is not one of its own user ports to
be foreign.  With assisted CPU-port learning enabled, a dynamically
learned address on such a port is therefore installed on the DSA CPU port.

That is wrong when another switchdev driver exposes a representor for the
same physical switch.  The bridge assigns both ports to the same hardware
domain, but DSA overwrites the address learned by the shared hardware with
a static CPU-port entry.  Hardware-forwarded traffic then follows the CPU
entry instead of the representor destination.

Use the physical parent ID to recognize bridge ports belonging to the same
switch.  Keep assisted learning for genuinely foreign ports.

Signed-off-by: Stijn Tintel <stijn@linux-ipv6.be>
---
 net/dsa/user.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/dsa/user.c
+++ b/net/dsa/user.c
@@ -3686,8 +3686,13 @@ static bool dsa_foreign_dev_check(const
 	if (netif_is_bridge_master(foreign_dev))
 		return !dsa_tree_offloads_bridge_dev(dst, foreign_dev);
 
-	if (netif_is_bridge_port(foreign_dev))
+	if (netif_is_bridge_port(foreign_dev)) {
+		if (netdev_port_same_parent_id((struct net_device *)dev,
+					       (struct net_device *)foreign_dev))
+			return false;
+
 		return !dsa_tree_offloads_bridge_port(dst, foreign_dev);
+	}
 
 	/* Everything else is foreign */
 	return true;
